BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meeting with Pol Pot
DTSTART:20250520T193000Z
DTEND:20250520T213500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T193000Z
UID:bvyAyPLWDL
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nOscar®-nominated filmmaker Rith
 y Panh (2013’s The Missing Picture) directs this historical drama that u
 nfolds like a horror film\, as three French journalists in 1978 Cambodia l
 earn the terrible truth about the Khmer Rouge regime. Learn about the Eliz
 abeth Becker Cambodia and Khmer Rouge Collection from UW Associate Profess
 or of Sociocultural Anthropology Jenna Grant at the May 18 screening. Spon
 sored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/meeting-with-pol-pot
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Joqtau
DTSTART:20250520T194500Z
DTEND:20250520T211000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T194500Z
UID:B7JkI8JbSR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 71 mins (1h11m)\n\nYoung Darkhan returns to his vill
 age after a seven-year absence to accompany his late grandfather on an ima
 gined journey to his ancestral home to learn the ways of his elders and th
 e gradual loss of their traditional customs and language. Sponsored by:\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/joqtau\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Film
  Center (Thu 22 May\, 6:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Luz
DTSTART:20250520T200000Z
DTEND:20250520T215500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T200000Z
UID:5cnQFyZdVV
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nA Chinese ex-con seeks to rekind
 le a relationship with his estranged cam girl daughter\, while a gallerist
  connects with her ailing French stepmother (Huppert)\, in this dual narra
 tive about finding familial intimacy in a virtual reality world. Sponsored
  by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/luz\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • AMC P
 acific Place 11 (Thu 22 May\, 6:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To Kill a Mongolian Horse
DTSTART:20250520T200000Z
DTEND:20250520T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T200000Z
UID:QVN3h4eveu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nIn this lovely and patient docudr
 ama set on the Mongolian steppes\, a champion horseback rider and herdsman
  struggles to maintain his family's ranch and traditional way of life in t
 he modern era.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/to-kill-a-mongolian-horse\
 n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jean Cocteau
DTSTART:20250520T220000Z
DTEND:20250520T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T220000Z
UID:VAC3450V83
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nLisa Immordino Vreeland (SIFF 202
 1’s Truman & Tennessee: An Intimate Conversation) constructs an astonish
 ing portrait of polymath Jean Cocteau—filmmaker\, playwright\, poet—to
 ld in his own words using his journals\, letters\, and artistic works. Pro
 ducer/Editor John Northrup scheduled to attend. Come early to the May 20 s
 creening to find out about ACT Contemporary Theatre's upcoming production 
 of "Twelfth Night" and get the chance to win a pair of tickets to the play
 !  Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/jean-cocteau\n\nFilm is 
 also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Evergreens
DTSTART:20250520T223000Z
DTEND:20250521T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T223000Z
UID:sKko0T3WrE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nIn Spokane-based Jared Briley’
 s directorial debut featuring a treasure trove of local talent\, young Eve
  (Darby Lee-Stack) and James (Edouard Philipponat) come of age as they roa
 d trip across the Evergreen State in this Washington-set love story. Write
 r/Director Jared Briley scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.
 siff.net/festival/evergreens\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:She’s The He
DTSTART:20250520T223000Z
DTEND:20250521T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T223000Z
UID:v85kCovBCf
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 81 mins (1h21m)\n\nFirst-time director Siobhan McCar
 thy put together a cast and crew of almost entirely trans\, nonbinary\, an
 d queer people to make this Bottoms-esque teen satire about two seniors wh
 o pretend to be trans during their last week of high school\, only for one
  of them to find it suits them just fine. Director Siobhan McCarthy\, prod
 ucer Vic Brandt\, and producer Halley Albert scheduled to attend. Keep the
  cinematic trans hijinks going with a chance to win tickets to the Queer &
  Trans Film Festival at the May 19 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www
 .siff.net/festival/shes-the-he\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Gloria of your Imagination
DTSTART:20250520T223000Z
DTEND:20250521T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T223000Z
UID:L6vpUyScXS
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nIn 1964\, a 30-year-old divorced 
 woman named Gloria was filmed consulting with three eminent therapists. Fi
 lmmaker Jennifer Reeves uses this footage to explore single parenthood\, g
 endered power relationships\, and Gloria’s remarkable story. Director Je
 nnifer Reeves and co-producer Randy Sterns scheduled to attend. Attend the
  May 20 screening to meet filmmaker Caryn Cline\, get a free zine from Int
 erbay Cinema Society\, and learn about the upcoming Engauge Experimental F
 ilm Festival. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-gloria-of
 -your-imagination\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Undercover
DTSTART:20250520T223000Z
DTEND:20250521T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T223000Z
UID:JAXyabLM4Q
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nA young policewoman is recruited
  to infiltrate the terrorist group ETA and dismantle one of their dangerou
 s commandos. The 2025 Goya Award winner for Best Film recreates an unknow
 n\, shocking\, and terrible true story that offers a testimony to dark and
  violent times that still ripple through today’s Spain. This film is gen
 erously sponsored by Dale Pratt. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fes
 tival/undercover
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:1-800-ON-HER-OWN
DTSTART:20250520T224500Z
DTEND:20250521T001500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T224500Z
UID:mPkNjsQTbM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 78 mins (1h18m)\n\nStrum a tune with indie folk sing
 er-songwriter and activist Ani DiFranco through the making of her 2021 alb
 um “Revolutionary Love\,” recorded in lockdown\, and the path she pave
 d for other female artists via her Righteous Babe Recordings record label.
  Meet the songwriters of Reel Songs Film Collective (@reelsongscollective)
  at the May 19 screening! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/1
 -800-on-her-own\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Freeing Juanita
DTSTART:20250521T003000Z
DTEND:20250521T015500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T003000Z
UID:wwSg9SZjmY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 74 mins (1h14m)\n\nAn Indigenous Maya Chuj couple ma
 ke a treacherous thousand-mile journey across Guatemala and into Mexico to
  demand the emancipation of their niece\, who was wrongfully imprisoned du
 ring her intended migration to the United States. Producer Tristan Call an
 d director's partner Caitlin Brzezinski scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:
 \n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/freeing-juanita\n\nAlso playing at:\n  
 • SIFF Film Center (Wed 21 May\, 3:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed
 .
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baby Doe
DTSTART:20250521T010000Z
DTEND:20250521T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T010000Z
UID:YW7B1g7efW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nNearly 30 years after Gail aband
 oned her newborn son in the woods and returned to her conservative Christi
 an life\, the police came and arrested her for infanticide. From Tribeca-w
 inning documentarian Jessica Earnshaw (Hulu’s “Jacinta”). Director J
 essica Earnshaw and co-producer John Rudolf scheduled to attend. Sponsored
  by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/baby-doe\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • 
 SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Wed 21 May\, 3:45 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blue Road: The Edna O'Brien Story
DTSTART:20250521T010000Z
DTEND:20250521T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T010000Z
UID:0BLI098PSR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nThe controversial and boldly fem
 inist Irish author Edna O’Brien (“The Country Girls”) shares journal
  entries and provocative insight into her trailblazing career in a series 
 of late-in-life interviews in this Palm Springs International Film Festiva
 l award winner. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/blue-road-t
 he-edna-obrien-story
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Come Closer
DTSTART:20250521T010000Z
DTEND:20250521T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T010000Z
UID:DacnlJHSIh
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 107 mins (1h47m)\n\nAfter Eden’s brother dies sudd
 enly\, she discovers that he had a secret girlfriend. As the two women get
  to know one another\, they embark on an intense and intimate relationship
  of their own.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/come-closer\n\nAlso playin
 g at:\n  • SIFF Film Center (Thu 22 May\, 3:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being
  streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drowned Land
DTSTART:20250521T010000Z
DTEND:20250521T024000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T010000Z
UID:w7UTIHtvPk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 86 mins (1h26m)\n\nThe Choctaw Nation of southeaster
 n Oklahoma fights against cultural displacement and the developers who wis
 h to dam and divert the Kiamichi River\, one of the most ecologically dive
 rse bodies of water in the state\, in this call to action from SIFF 4th Wo
 rld Media Lab alum Colleen Thurston. Director Colleen Thurston\, cinematog
 rapher Charles Elmore\, and protagonist Charlotte Robbins scheduled to att
 end. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/drowned-land\n\nFilm i
 s also being streamed.
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monarch City
DTSTART:20250521T013000Z
DTEND:20250521T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T013000Z
UID:sN0ptlBnqM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 70 mins (1h10m)\n\nIn this soulful family drama shot
  in and around the Cascades\, a young adult in rural America must confront
  her family’s numerous hardships—addiction\, incarceration\, poverty
 —and find the grace in life’s most fragile moments. Director Titus Ric
 hard scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/m
 onarch-city\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Wed 21 
 May\, 3:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SIFF & CFC Present The Dark Crystal with DJ NicFit
DTSTART:20250521T013000Z
DTEND:20250521T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T013000Z
UID:ZyCoWJibT5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nJoin the Gelflings (and Fizzgig!)
  on their quest to defeat the evil Skeksis in this very special presentati
 on of The Dark Crystal. This time\, Seattle’s own DJ NicFit will create 
 a live soundtrack to accompany Jim Henson and Frank Oz’s cult 1982 fanta
 sy adventure. Classified Cinema will be giving out stickers and film poste
 rs made exclusively for this one-time-only event in the lobby before the s
 how! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/siff-and-cfc-present-t
 he-dark-crystal-with-dj-nicfit
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:By the Stream
DTSTART:20250521T030000Z
DTEND:20250521T050500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T030000Z
UID:KASNouKYcB
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 111 mins (1h51m)\n\nHong Sang-soo (Our Sunhi) is bac
 k at SIFF with another meditative\, lo-fi rumination on the creation of ar
 t\, as a university lecturer calls upon her retired uncle to write and dir
 ect a play for her students after their previous hire left under a cloud o
 f scandal. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/by-the-stream\n\
 nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Wed 21 May\, 12:30 PM
 )
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Don’t Let’s Go to the Dogs Tonight
DTSTART:20250521T033000Z
DTEND:20250521T052000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T033000Z
UID:LIBIDmYytA
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nActress Embeth Davidtz (Schindler
 's List) makes her feature directorial debut\, adapting Alexandra Fuller
 ’s bestselling memoir about a precocious eight-year-old farmgirl who wit
 nesses Rhodesia’s tumultuous political shift in the early 1980s. Sponsor
 ed by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/dont-lets-go-to-the-dogs-tonight
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Transfers
DTSTART:20250521T033000Z
DTEND:20250521T051000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T033000Z
UID:MwgpRRGMEQ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nA poignant documentary that uses 
 testimonials\, archival material\, animations\, and heartbreaking reenactm
 ents to chronicle Argentina’s onetime military dictatorship’s use of t
 he infamous Death Flights\, one of the most brutal and effective ways of k
 illing and disappearing people. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fest
 ival/transfers\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Under the Volcano
DTSTART:20250521T033000Z
DTEND:20250521T052500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T033000Z
UID:cMCevkVBlb
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nA Ukrainian family on vacation i
 n the Canary Islands suddenly find themselves stranded upon Russia’s inv
 asion of their home country\, sending them into fits of desperation and in
 trospection as they wander the beaches speculating what comes next.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/under-the-volcano\n\nFilm is also being streame
 d.
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Home Sweet Home
DTSTART:20250521T034500Z
DTEND:20250521T055000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T034500Z
UID:SVqSg97qcF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nSingle mother Sofie starts a new
  career as a caretaker for the elderly\, only to be humbled by the toll it
  takes on her physical and mental state\, in this authentic and rewarding 
 glimpse at the uncelebrated world of healthcare workers from SIFF alum Fre
 lle Petersen. Director Frelle Petersen and actor Jette Søndergaard schedu
 led to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/home-sweet-h
 ome\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Wed 21 May\, 3:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:By Design
DTSTART:20250521T040000Z
DTEND:20250521T054000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T040000Z
UID:OD35ZSmSLb
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nPlayful provocateur Amanda Kramer
  (Please Baby Please\, SIFF 2024’s So Unreal) has crafted another audaci
 ous\, performance art-based piece of absurdist satire about fetish and des
 ire\, as a lonely woman (Juliette Lewis) swaps bodies with a chair\, only 
 to finally find comfort in life. Cast member Alisa Torres scheduled to att
 end. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/by-design\n\nAlso play
 ing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (Wed 21 May\, 4:30 PM)\n\nFilm i
 s also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Riefenstahl
DTSTART:20250521T040000Z
DTEND:20250521T061000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T040000Z
UID:kERnfFfUbP
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nA gripping portrait of controver
 sial filmmaker and propagandist Leni Riefenstahl (The Triumph of the Will)
 \, who despite all evidence to the contrary still maintained she was not c
 omplicit in the atrocities carried out by the Third Reich. Sponsored by:\n
 \nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/riefenstahl\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIF
 F Cinema Uptown House 1 (Thu 22 May\, 12:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
