SUMMARY:By the Stream
DTSTART:20250521T193000Z
DTEND:20250521T213500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T193000Z
UID:nX6rfgujXW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 111 mins (1h51m)\n\nHong Sang-soo (Our Sunhi) is bac
 k at SIFF with another meditative\, lo-fi rumination on the creation of ar
 t\, as a university lecturer calls upon her retired uncle to write and dir
 ect a play for her students after their previous hire left under a cloud o
 f scandal. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/by-the-stream\n\
 nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Tue 20 May\, 8:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Am Nevenka
DTSTART:20250521T200000Z
DTEND:20250521T220500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T200000Z
UID:ejwY3MthTk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nNevenka Fernández\, the town’
 s finance councilor\, is relentlessly pursued by the mayor\, a man used to
  always getting what he wants politically and personally. Nevenka decides 
 to report him\, turning her courageous fight into Spain’s first #MeToo c
 ase. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/i-am-nevenka\n\nAlso p
 laying at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Fri 23 May\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fly Me to the Moon
DTSTART:20250521T203000Z
DTEND:20250521T223500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T203000Z
UID:feY8hmNNWq
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nIn Sasha Chuk’s autobiographic
 al coming-of-age drama\, young Yuen struggles to adapt to her new surround
 ings and social class when she and her mother emigrate from Mainland China
  to 1990s Hong Kong to reunite with the family patriarch. Sponsored by:\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/fly-me-to-the-moon\n\nFilm is also being st
 reamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Khartoum
DTSTART:20250521T203000Z
DTEND:20250521T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T203000Z
UID:eZfFiux9CF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nThe Sudanese Civil War has displa
 ced over 10 million of its citizens. Now\, five survivors contend with the
 ir own memories\, and hope for a peaceful future\, using green screen tech
 nology to reenact their lives leading up to the military coup that forced 
 their evacuation. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/khartoum
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:40 Acres
DTSTART:20250521T220000Z
DTEND:20250522T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T220000Z
UID:7iAUDv91vh
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nMusic video veteran R.T. Thorne 
 directs SAG nominee Danielle Deadwyler (The Piano Lesson) in this TIFF sen
 sation\, a speculative fiction thriller about a Black family in a starved\
 , post-civil war near future who must defend their farm from invading cann
 ibals. Before the screening\, stop by the lobby to explore merch and mater
 ials from Offbeat Films production company and learn more about their crea
 tive work. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/40-acres
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
