DTEND:20250525T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T013000Z
UID:rsa7Fe7VWT
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nSeattle loves its sushi\, but did
  you know the cuisine’s North American popularity is thanks to a man nam
 ed Hidekazu Tojo? Learn the story of the chef who changed the world after 
 moving from Japan to Vancouver in the 1970s\, staying true to his traditio
 ns despite all odds. Director Mads Baekkevold\, producer Matthew Dix\, and
  subject Chef Hidekazu Tojo scheduled to attend. Lovers of Japanese food a
 nd baked goods won't want to miss our trivia giveaway of gift cards to Sai
 nt Bread and The Wayland Mill at the May 25 screening! Sponsored by:\n\nht
 tps://www.siff.net/festival/the-chef-and-the-daruma\n\nAlso playing at:\n 
  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (Sun 25 May\, 2:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
